title: The Red Army on the Border
subtitle: Soviet cavalry waters its horses within sight of East Prussia.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 9 and crisis = 0 and warsaw_outcome = 2 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Soviet cavalry on the East Prussian border', 3);
// what a rising could put into the field
Q.e20_rising_strength = Q.red_guards_strength + Q.militancy / 2 + Q.worker_support / 2 + (Q.ruhr_red_army == 2 ? 20 : 0) + (Q.border_rising == 1 ? 10 : 0);
!}

= The Red Army on the Border

Soviet Poland is three weeks old. Its Red Army is hungry, and its supply lines run back four hundred miles to Smolensk. It stands on the borders of East Prussia and Silesia.

Seeckt has moved Reichswehr divisions east. The Entente demands that French troops be allowed to cross Germany to the Vistula. Radek writes from Moscow: this is the hour.

- @rise: Rise now, and open the road to the east.
- @no_soldier: Campaign for not one soldier and not one train against Soviet Russia.

@rise
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] [? if e20_rising_strength >= 80 : Central Germany may hold for a while. ?][? if e20_rising_strength < 80 : We are not strong enough, and the Reichswehr knows it. ?]
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.border_rising = 2;
Q.e20_rising_held = Q.e20_rising_strength >= 80 ? 1 : 0;
Q.repression += Q.e20_rising_held ? 10 : 25;
Q.red_guards_strength *= Q.e20_rising_held ? 0.8 : 0.4;
RG.district('halle', {members: Q.e20_rising_held ? -0.05 : -0.2, militancy: 10});
Q.world_revolution += Q.e20_rising_held ? 8 : 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

The signal goes out on 5 September. Armed miners occupy the pits and the railway junctions of Halle-Merseburg and the Mansfeld copper country. [? if e20_rising_held = 1 : For a week no Reichswehr train passes through Central Germany. Then the miners go home with their rifles, and the government agrees that no Entente soldier will cross the Reich. ?][? if e20_rising_held = 0 : In four days it is over. The Security Police storm the works with armoured cars. The Red Army does not move. ?]

@no_soldier
subtitle: Rallies under the banners of all three workers' parties.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The railwaymen's union declares that no Entente troop train will cross Germany. The government, relieved, says the same.
